    <string name="os_host">Host (where the computing power is)</string>
    <string name="os_host_opis">Your home network, or your own server outside the house</string>
    <string name="os_host_doma">Home network</string>
    <string name="os_host_vprasanje">By default the host is at home: Safeer Link runs on this TV and the files come from your computer in the same house - nothing leaves your network.\n\nYou can also use your own server outside the house (a rented or cloud machine). Then the TV connects to it over the internet: pairing is the same as at home (a code, and the certificate is pinned), but the traffic - including your files - leaves your home network and travels to that server. Only use a server you control.</string>
    <string name="os_host_vnesi">Enter an address</string>
    <string name="os_host_naslov">Address of your server</string>
    <string name="os_host_naslov_opis">Name or IP address, with a port if it is not the usual one. Example: moj-streznik.si or 203.0.113.7:8990</string>
    <string name="os_host_naslov_namig">moj-streznik.si</string>
    <string name="os_host_naslov_napaka">That does not look like an address. Example: moj-streznik.si</string>
    <string name="os_host_povezujem">Connecting to the server…</string>
    <string name="os_host_koda">Code from the server</string>
    <string name="os_host_koda_opis">Safeer Link on that server shows a code. Type it here. The code never travels over the network; both sides only prove they know it.</string>
    <string name="os_host_koda_namig">code from the screen</string>
    <string name="os_host_poveziSe">Connect</string>
    <string name="os_host_povezan">Connected to %1$s. Files and commands now travel over the internet to your server.</string>
    <string name="os_host_napacna_koda">Wrong code, or someone else is in between. Try again.</string>
    <string name="os_host_prevec_poskusov">Too many attempts. Start the pairing again on the server.</string>
    <string name="os_host_ni_odgovora">The server did not answer. Check the address, that Safeer Link is running on it and that the port is open.</string>
    <string name="os_host_oddaljen_vprasanje">The host is %1$s, outside your home network. Go back to the home network? The token for that server is forgotten; you can pair again at any time.</string>
    <string name="os_host_domov">Back to the home network</string>
    <string name="os_host_spet_doma">The host is the home network again.</string>
    <string name="os_zaganjalnik_televizor_obdrzi">The TV keeps its own</string>
    <string name="os_zaganjalnik_televizor_obdrzi_opis">Safeer OS is switched on as the home screen, but this television does not hand the Home key over: the manufacturer routes it to its own home screen (%1$s). That is the TV\'s doing, not a fault in Safeer OS, and without changing the TV\'s firmware it cannot be worked around.\n\nSafeer OS still opens from the launcher, from the apps row and with the Safeer Link remote. You can leave this on (it costs nothing) or switch it off.</string>
    <string name="os_zaganjalnik_izklopi_kratko">Switch off</string>
    <string name="os_zaganjalnik_sistemske">TV settings</string>
    <string name="os_zagon">Start when the TV turns on</string>
    <string name="os_zagon_opis">Safeer OS is the first screen after you switch the television on</string>
    <string name="os_zagon_vprasanje">When the television starts, Safeer OS opens full screen, so it is the first thing you see. Nothing on the television is changed: the Home key still goes wherever it goes today, and you can switch this off at any time.</string>
    <string name="os_zagon_kanal">Safeer OS - start after switching on</string>
